    "created_at": "2019-09-27T12:57:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-09-27T12:57:17Z",
    "body": "> https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-mixed-content/level2.html does help and would thwart the attack described on the WebKit blog. Attackers could still play with navigations, but that's much more visible.\r\n\r\nAs pointed out by Matt, auto upgrade of passive mixed content only fixes the problem on HTTPS pages. HSTS super cookies still work on HTTP pages.",
