    "created_at": "2020-05-19T13:51:50Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-05-19T13:52:27Z",
    "body": "> @johnwilander thanks, and now that you block cross-site cookies, does that mean no cross-site fetch will have HSTS upgrading? Do you do anything special for HSTS preloads?\r\n\r\nThe logic is still that if cookies are blocked for a cross-site load, then (dynamic) HSTS is ignored. Since all cross-site cookies are blocked by default, so is cross-site (dynamic) HSTS.\r\n\r\nI write dynamic HSTS above since the preload list is always respected. Preloaded HSTS cannot be used for setting a super cookie.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
